BACKGROUND: The `Proxy` middleware panics when its balancer has zero targets. `roundRobinBalancer.Next` does `b.i = b.i % uint32(len(b.targets))` which is an integer divide-by-zero panic when there are no targets; `randomBalancer.Next` does `b.targets[b.random.Intn(len(b.targets))]` which panics with `invalid argument to Intn`. Also, `ProxyWithConfig`'s handler does not handle a nil target returned by `Balancer.Next`. Expected behavior: a request through a Proxy whose balancer has no targets must NOT panic and must return an error (502 Bad Gateway).

